{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/14879-making-fae-lords-titles-tells-hints-etc","id":14879,"title":"Making Fae Lords, Titles, Tells, Hints, etc.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-20T14:22:36-08:00","id":14879,"title":"Making Fae Lords, Titles, Tells, Hints, etc.","content":"Hi,<br /> <br /> I'm brainstorming ideas and I want to make a Fae Lord as an antagonist for a group of PCs. The game has the PCs as Mage Archmasters sending 'lesser' supernatural agents in to achieve any random variety if tasks to fulfill their Omens. The Archmasters are more a framing device to allow for disparate plots, crossovers and shenanigans to make 'sense'.<br /> <br /> So, a True Fae is likely to be an enemy they will face.<br /> <br /> But I was wondering if anyone had made a true fae and had suggestions, hints, experiences etc. with them and would be willing to share. I have many questions and probably more will come as I think of them but for now...<br /> <br /> 1. how many titles should a true fae have?<br /> 2. how many can they have?<br /> 3. example titles?<br /> 4. what makes good tells?<br /> 5. how to drop hints about them?<br /> 6. how to drop hints about weaknesses? (the whole issue of the ST thinking they've made it obvious but the players missing it entirely)<br /> 7. what is a good number of titles to give them?<br /> 8. can actors/props/wisps be affected by mind control/reading/manipulation powers? How about body/material/etc. alteration powers?<br /> 9. where do titles come from?<br /> 10. are new ones created? if so how?<br /> 11. are there instead a fixed number number of them being fought over and captured and traded etc.?<br /> 12. if there are a fixed number how many? ballpark?<br /> 13. how many true fae are there? ballpark?<br /> <br /> <br /> Aside from questions, making pacts, deals, contracts, etc. with players...sounds really difficult...if I am talking as a true fae and want to offer a deal or suggest a different pact that has loopholes and such for the fae lord's favour...how do I do that? I don't know how to make watertight deals. Any hints of suggestions on how to get around this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","user":"Scutarii","date":". 11-20-2013, 05:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T14:38:53-08:00","id":14888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/14879-making-fae-lords-titles-tells-hints-etc#post14879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. how many titles should a true fae have?</div> </div> </div> </div>Game of Immortals weighs the starting counts toward two and four, but can conceivably run the gamut from one to five.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. how many can they have? </div> </div> </div>Five before they hit Wyrd Ascension by the default count, though that number is subject to individual-game jiggering.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 9. where do titles come from? </div> </div> </div>Description of Fae by other Fae.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 10. are new ones created? if so how? </div> </div> </div>The consumption of a Fae's name by another Fae transforms it into a Title which a third Fae describes and consequently gets the right to fight its holder for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 13. how many true fae are there? ballpark? </div> </div> </div>Literally numberless.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Aside from questions, making pacts, deals, contracts, etc. with players...sounds really difficult...if I am talking as a true fae and want to offer a deal or suggest a different pact that has loopholes and such for the fae lord's favour...how do I do that? I don't know how to make watertight deals. Any hints of suggestions on how to get around this? </div> </div> </div>Having come up with at least two chronicle ideas whose ultimate inciting incidents amounted to &quot;a couple of Fae had a bet going,&quot; stick to broad outlines and important rules and add in details as investigation requires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T15:03:51-08:00","id":14894,"title":"","content":"What is Wyrd Ascension?<br /> <br /> Broad outlines of deals probably won't cut it for Jon...he'll want clause and subclause to peruse and poke...<br /> <br /> I could mechanically make it some extended task with a silly high number of succeses to find a hole and time increments of months but...that still doesn't seem right as clever mortals should be able to outwit the fae...unless they're only outwitting an Actor.<br /> <br /> What if the scene is culminating in the players making the fae an offer or vice versa, the deal has to be made in real time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T16:09:09-08:00","id":14935,"title":"","content":"Example titles: The Shape in the Dark, the King of the Cracked Mirror, The Abyssal Hunger, The Caress That Brings Ruination, The Clavinger, The Argent Flame ... I prefer my titles abstract, Note these are not necessarily what the True Fae goes by day to day. <br /> <br /> For fun, try to create each in your head as an Actor, Prop and a Realm.<br /> <br /> When it comes to weaknesses, I prefer to link them intimately to the True Fae's MO somehow. The Trua Fae that often appears as a preacher? Hates church bells. The one that comes to you in mirrors? Broken mirror shards are its Bane. The one that tries to make you its perfect lover? Genuine affection hurts it and the tears of the heartbroken burn its skin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T20:12:35-08:00","id":15076,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">I created three true fae which I posted up on my blog \u2013 titles and information on those titles included. <a href=\"http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/2013/03/london-fae-spotlight-red-queen.html\" target=\"_blank\">Red Queen</a>, <a href=\"http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/2013/05/london-fae-spotlight-jack-frost.html\" target=\"_blank\">Jack Frost</a> and the <a href=\"http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/2013/04/the-snow-princess-summary.html\" target=\"_blank\">Snow Princess</a>. The Red Queen and Snow Princess both have an Actor, Prop, Wisps and an Arcadian Realm while Jack Frost has the first three but lacks an Arcadian Realm. I did this because his core concept was based around the idea of being a landless Peter Pan / Doctor Who type figure who took kids away on adventures into other people\u2019s realms. If he gained more titles, he would simply gain more Props rather than bother with a Locale.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">A True Fae can have a huge amount of titles, though I like to imagine that the average one had between 3 \u2013 4. I don\u2019t know if canon says any different, however. 3 \u2013 4 seems good to me.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Since Actors / Wisps have resistance stats, I\u2019d have them roll against mind control. It\u2019s not that a character would be mind controlling them, per se, but it\u2019d be part of the \u2018deal\u2019 and the \u2018laws\u2019 that the Actors / Wisps are submitting to which would allow them to be mentally coerced. They\u2019d know the whole time, however, which means they could subvert it in interesting ways while obeying the letter of the law of the powers.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">I imagine there are tens of thousands of titles and that each one is a separate part of some larger \u2018entity\u2019. Changelings don\u2019t discover titles when they hit Wyrd 10. They\u2019re summoned by the Arcadian mass of abandoned titles and then penetrated and possessed by one, becoming its tool, as without a human mind \u2013 even a badly torn apart one \u2013 a Fae would lack even its own rudimentary creativity and ability to follow or comprehend stories. But that\u2019s my personal opinion.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My horror roleplaying blog with a strong focus on World of Darkness and Call of Cthulhu can be found here: <a href=\"http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/\" target=\"_blank\">http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1248-laraqua","name":"Laraqua","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T11:14:32-08:00","id":15484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Laraqua</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/14879-making-fae-lords-titles-tells-hints-etc?p=15076#post15076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">I imagine there are tens of thousands of titles and that each one is a separate part of some larger \u2018entity\u2019. Changelings don\u2019t discover titles when they hit Wyrd 10. They\u2019re summoned by the Arcadian mass of abandoned titles and then penetrated and possessed by one, becoming its tool, as without a human mind \u2013 even a badly torn apart one \u2013 a Fae would lack even its own rudimentary creativity and ability to follow or comprehend stories. But that\u2019s my personal opinion.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>In my headcanon they don't have any Titles yet and function as True Fae with no Titles, just their Name, feuding to get more and grow stronger. Though I'm not sure how that squares with their Wyrd - does it drop to 5 or does this Name have an unusually potent Wyrd, at least for a time? ST's call, as always.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T23:03:38-08:00","id":15912,"title":"","content":"Hmm, can only a True Fae have a title? Or could something else (say...a PC) that has defeated the particular manifestation of the Title claim it? If so how?<br /> <br /> I rather like the idea of some PC playing a Mummy gaining a really incongruous Title from some Fae Lord that stole a Relic <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T00:19:07-08:00","id":15931,"title":"","content":"According to rumors, the only Changelings to attain Titles were the four that made the contracts with the seasons.<br /> So it could be possible, if epic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T13:27:25-08:00","id":16254,"title":"","content":"My own headcanon is that if a changeling managed to get a Title, they would start the process of transforming into a True Fae almost immediately; their Clarity would nosedive, and their Wyrd would slowly rise, and they would cast aside their mortal bodies and take up their places as Lords of Arcadia. (This was actually a major NPC's plan in the first Changeling game that I ran; pretending to be a loyalist to maneuver his master into a position to be destroyed, and then assume his Titles and replace him.<br /> <br /> Weirdly, the plan was successful, as my players never suspected him of anything until the fateful transformation occurred. They just thought they were going to kill a Gentry...)<br /> <br /> My headcanon also doesn't have changelings automatically go Gentry at Wyrd 10, but if it did, I would assume that their mortality and nature, as it boils away, transforms into their first Title - a short description of the person that they once were, which they now wear like a fine suit over a raging maelstrom of Wyrd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Remember - popcorn can feel pain.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1195-frivyeti","name":"FrivYeti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T17:12:49-08:00","id":16346,"title":"","content":"I like to think Changelings can get Titles because it leads to interesting stories about power and what your willing to give up to get it. What kind of sacrifices does someone have to make to get that Title? Using a lot of the powers a Title gives you requires you to be in Arcadia, which is not safe, even if your Title grants you protection and theoretically Gentry status. Everyone will see you as an easy target, both in Arcadia and on Earth. And all of this is going to rip your Clarity to shreds.<br /> <br /> What are you willing to do for power? End the end, is it worth it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T18:05:43-08:00","id":16376,"title":"","content":"Isn't there something about Wyrd 10 Changelings having to regularly roll to avoid becoming 'strange', killing those who try to hold them back as they obssess with their thoughts of the Fae Lands, and rushing off to Arcadia? There's a tale of a woodblood suddenly becoming all the more alien in appearance before rushing off. In my head canon, I've taken that to mean the eventual fate of Changelings who attain Wyrd 10 is Death or True Faedom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My horror roleplaying blog with a strong focus on World of Darkness and Call of Cthulhu can be found here: <a href=\"http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/\" target=\"_blank\">http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1248-laraqua","name":"Laraqua","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T18:33:46-08:00","id":16393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FrivYeti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/14879-making-fae-lords-titles-tells-hints-etc?p=16254#post16254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My headcanon also doesn't have changelings automatically go Gentry at Wyrd 10</div> </div> </div> </div>Because Blore's assumptions getting proliferated annoys me:<br /> <br /> That's not your headcanon. That is the default state of affairs. Becoming Nightmare kicks in at a player- and Storyteller-determined point <i>after</i> hitting Wyrd 10. Dancers in the Dusk renders it as starting when you hit Wyrd 10, but that's because it's mentioning the rule in a tiny sidebar about using the rule in combination with a systems hack whereby Wyrd can be rapidly gained and lost and there's only so much threat frailties can add to a gain by that point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T08:24:24-08:00","id":16649,"title":"","content":"The process in Equinox Road is not portrayed as instant, but I certainly read it as being inevitable for all Wyrd 10 changelings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Remember - popcorn can feel pain.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1195-frivyeti","name":"FrivYeti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T12:01:53-08:00","id":16720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FrivYeti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/14879-making-fae-lords-titles-tells-hints-etc?p=16649#post16649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The process in Equinox Road is not portrayed as instant, but I certainly read it as being inevitable for all Wyrd 10 changelings.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/4464486/becomingnightmaretiming.png\" target=\"_blank\">And I do not</a>, because a) reading it as inevitable says terrible things about its utility as a metaphor for the abused becoming an abuser (because that isn't an inevitability or even a common occurrence), b) it being inevitable gives the Fae a reliable means of reproduction despite all statements to the contrary about their fecundity, and c) parallel examples in other templates \u2014 archmages, Methuselahs, deathlords at a stretch \u2014 aren't a matter of hitting Supernatural Tolerance 10 and waiting either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T15:05:15-08:00","id":16815,"title":"","content":"To be fair, very few changelings will ever reach Wyrd 10, it's preventable by lowering your Wyrd back down to 9 and going True Fae isn't the same as becoming a a deathlord, etc. It's not gained through age or knowledge or revelation. You've just strengthened your intimate connexion to a realm of madness too strongly.<br /> <br /> Your point about abuser becoming abused and fecundity are valid, though. That said, I don't think True Fae intend for this. They're not trying to reproduce like a parasitic wasp. In a sense, the changeling has a choice, though - Wyrd, under normal rules, only rises with XP. You choose to raise it. At high Wyrd you're very inhuman and laden with frailties. You choose to keep going. You choose, without quite realising it, to become True fae, and that's the horror. The Wyrd never cares if you understood the choice, only that you made it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":452,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","user":"Eremite","date":". 11-23-2013, 07:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T16:06:31-08:00","id":16849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/14879-making-fae-lords-titles-tells-hints-etc?p=16815#post16815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, very few changeling will ever reach Wyrd 10, it's preventable by lowering your Wyrd back down to 9 and going Truae Fae isn't the same as becoming a True Fae, a deathlord, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lowering Wyrd takes months of weening the character off to a lesser degree of Glamour addiction and is called out as the primary means of halting the process, the two primary instances of Methuselahs (the Lambton Worm isn't outright called one, but Alice is directed to interview it on the basis of its possession of a quality only Methuselahs have among the Kindred) both used different processes to become what they were that nevertheless both involved their &quot;death,&quot; the Threshold involves changes that essentially uproot your existence from your history (and Ascension goes further than that), and becoming Fae is essentially the death knell of your humanity as one of the Lost.<br /> <br /> They're not <i>the same</i>, but they are <i>damn similar</i> in all the regards that matter \u2014 you can have high-BP Kindred that never become Methuselahs and high-Gnosis magi never seek the Threshold, and it strikes me as rather dull to say that there's no such thing as a Wyrd 10 Lost who'll never trigger the waking dreams of the Jeweled Realm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They're not trying to reproduce like a parasitic wasp. </div> </div> </div>True \u2014 the mentions of things like &quot;a changeling is reminded of their Keeper every time they look in a mirror&quot; would suggest it's more akin to playing god (moreso than usual, anyway) by altering life in their own image as part of their lack of innate boundaries between Self and Other. Regardless, the point at which a changeling becomes a True Fae seems to be set up in such a manner that whatever remained of the character's human soul is gone and all that remains is the bits of storybook logic they've built up around themselves. Whether they become a new Fae or just shore up their Keeper's Name or Title, the process is too much of a solid gain for Faerie to really say that &quot;inevitable for Wyrd 10 changelings&quot; is enough of a mitigating factor for a group that can be encouraged to seek more power simply by the appearance of an unearthly threat and the nature of Courtly culture (even <i>Winter</i> doesn't seem to discourage raising Wyrd despite its attractive effect on the Fae).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In a sense, the changeling has a chocie, though - Wyrd, under normal rules, only rises with XP. You choose to raise it. </div> </div> </div>And in the narrative accompanying that expenditure, that choice manifests primarily as continued and regular exercise of the advantages that fae existence affords you \u2014 a carrot that is accompanied by the stick of needing increasingly frequent infusions of Glamour to live as you continue to raise your Wyrd. When factoring in the heightened emotional responses of the Lost, hitting the point where, say, your kith redoubles upon itself is sort of a point of no return as far as power-tripping goes \u2014 lowering Wyrd would seem to all but <i>necessitate</i> an intervention by then.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At high Wyrd you're very inhuman and laden with frailties. You choose to keep going. You choose, without quite realsing it, to become True fae, and that's the horror. The Wyrd never cares if you understood the choice, only that you made it. </div> </div> </div>Problem being that the dreams that precipitate the Clarity-dive are stronger than even the normal vivid dreams of Arcadia that come with Wyrd 10, and the narrative logic the Wyrd deals in would seem to call for an inciting incident to kick off that last leap toward tragedy instead of it being a thing that Just Happens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 11-23-2013, 07:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T00:38:38-08:00","id":16988,"title":"","content":"But then the narrative of someone at Wyrd 10 striving to reduce it to avoid being consumed by the Fae is a good one too so surely some of the narrative causality could bleed over making it so the transition to True Fae does not just happen arbitrarily but if something within that Changeling's narrative causes them to slip from the path of dropping to Wyrd 9?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T11:51:23-08:00","id":17199,"title":"","content":"Considering their humanity you have to imagine there'd be changelings who are willing to turn because they believe they'll be different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-24-2013, 06:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T07:47:33-08:00","id":17701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/14879-making-fae-lords-titles-tells-hints-etc?p=16720#post16720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/4464486/becomingnightmaretiming.png\" target=\"_blank\">And I do not</a>, because a) reading it as inevitable says terrible things about its utility as a metaphor for the abused becoming an abuser (because that isn't an inevitability or even a common occurrence), b) it being inevitable gives the Fae a reliable means of reproduction despite all statements to the contrary about their fecundity, and c) parallel examples in other templates \u2014 archmages, Methuselahs, deathlords at a stretch \u2014 aren't a matter of hitting Supernatural Tolerance 10 and waiting either.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the most important part is D) It is specifically optional and not a forced mechanic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T15:50:07-08:00","id":21331,"title":"","content":"Yeah, very much a Your Mileage May Vary situation. I have it as a possibility but not an inevitability. If only 1 in 500 Changelings hit Wyrd 10 then only 1 in 10 Wyrd 10 Changelings become a True Fae. Considering how rare Changelings can be comparatively, that 1 in 5000 rate (apologies if my math is wrong) is quite rare indeed. The sort of thing legends are made of. Just enough to replace the True Fae who are destroyed when their last title is taken from them by another True Fae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My horror roleplaying blog with a strong focus on World of Darkness and Call of Cthulhu can be found here: <a href=\"http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/\" target=\"_blank\">http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1248-laraqua","name":"Laraqua","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T17:18:29-08:00","id":45931,"title":"","content":"I used to prefer to consider it an inevitability due to the extreme XP costs of getting to 10 in something before GMC. Now that the costs have been flattened I find it increasingly obvious that it may be worth considering Satchel's perspective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T15:45:54-07:00","id":991153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FrivYeti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/14879-making-fae-lords-titles-tells-hints-etc?p=16254#post16254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My own headcanon is that if a changeling managed to get a Title, they would start the process of transforming into a True Fae almost immediately; their Clarity would nosedive, and their Wyrd would slowly rise, and they would cast aside their mortal bodies and take up their places as Lords of Arcadia. (This was actually a major NPC's plan in the first Changeling game that I ran; pretending to be a loyalist to maneuver his master into a position to be destroyed, and then assume his Titles and replace him.<br /> <br /> Weirdly, the plan was successful, as my players never suspected him of anything until the fateful transformation occurred. They just thought they were going to kill a Gentry...)<br /> <br /> My headcanon also doesn't have changelings automatically go Gentry at Wyrd 10, but if it did, I would assume that their mortality and nature, as it boils away, transforms into their first Title - a short description of the person that they once were, which they now wear like a fine suit over a raging maelstrom of Wyrd.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is similar to my interpretation, except I keep a clause that splitting up the Title can happen to create an Entitlement, each Entitlement being a hard won price from the True Fae, and it also explains why the True Fae want to snatch up as many Entitled changelings as they can, there is likely a clause if all changelings of an Entitlement are recaptured or die then the one holding the most gains the Title as a trophy.<br /> <br /> This does keep the Abused become the Abuser valid, doesn't cause actual reproduction but is closer to recycling which is really what stories do, and make it not inevitable but a tragic ending due to the moral failing of not splitting up the power to avoid <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/HeWhoFightsMonsters\" target=\"_blank\">a fate worse than death</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 10-21-2016, 06:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}